# Post-task code review gate (AutoPulse)

Before finalizing any implementation, run a short code review pass on changed files focused on regressions and production risk.

## Review priorities (highest first)

- Correctness regressions in touched behavior and edge cases.
- Security/privacy regressions (API keys, tokens, PII capture/logging, auth scope).
- Performance regressions on hot paths (`POST /ingest`, SDK middleware/send path, dashboard critical loads).
- Product-scope drift from MVP boundaries in `DEVELOPMENT.md`.
- Missing or weak tests for behavior that changed.

## Project-specific checks

- Backend: keep ingest fast, authenticated, and project-scoped; validate normalized event fields.
- SDK: preserve non-blocking/silent-failure behavior and re-raise original exceptions after capture.
- Frontend: preserve fast diagnosis UX; avoid disruptive refresh/loading regressions after first paint.
- Jobs/retention paths: verify scheduler/metrics assumptions when related code is touched.

## Reporting format in final response

- List findings first, ordered by severity; include file paths and concrete risk.
- If no findings, state that clearly and call out any remaining test gaps or residual risk.
- Include tests/checks run and a concise manual verification section.
